# FENE-P 3D planar-extension analytical canary for the KRK-VE-3D dispatch.
# The production driver (run_viscoelastic_fvfd_extensional_3d) imposes the
# planar-extension velocity field u = (epsilon_dot*x, -epsilon_dot*y, 0) on a
# coarse box and advances psi = log(C) to the fixed point. No obstacle or
# inflow/outflow geometry is needed: velocity_mode=:imposed.
#
# The FENE-P (Peterlin) closure multiplies the relaxation by
#   f = (L² - 3) / (L² - tr C),
# capping the polymer trace below L² = Lmax2 (finite extensibility). At
# lambda = 50 and epsilon_dot = 0.005 (lambda*epsilon_dot = 0.25), Oldroyd-B
# would reach C_xx = 1/(1 - 2*lambda*epsilon_dot) = 2.0; the finite spring
# reduces this stretch (C_xx < 2) while keeping tr C < L². As Lmax2 → ∞ the
# result recovers the Oldroyd-B planar-extension fixed point.
# beta = nu_s/(nu_s+nu_p) = 0.5 with nu_total = 0.1.
Simulation extensional_fenep D3Q19

Define epsilon_dot = 0.005

Domain L = 24 x 24 x 6  N = 24 x 24 x 6
Physics epsilon_dot = epsilon_dot
Rheology fene_p { nu_s = 0.05 nu_p = 0.05 lambda = 50 Lmax2 = 50 }
Module viscoelastic

Run 1000 steps
